    "wacc_rationale": "USD flows, USD rate. Risk-free ~4.3% (10y UST), ERP 5.0%, beta ~0.9 -> cost of equity ~8.8%. Pre-tax cost of debt ~4.0% (FY2025 interest expense $607M on ~$16B average debt), ~3.2% after tax. Market weights ~88% equity ($105B) / 12% debt ($14.9B) -> ~8.1%; rounded up to 8.25%. Same WACC in all three scenarios: risk is charged through the scenario paths and weights, not a premium.",
    "lease_treatment": "US GAAP operating leases (~$205M/yr expense, $504M liability at 2026-06-30) sit inside operating expense and therefore inside EBITDA; the lease liability is NOT added to net debt. One treatment, charged once.",
    "nci_treatment": "No material non-controlling interest.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF (component route), routed via dcf-methods SKILL.md as a US operating company (medical devices: MedSurg & Neurotechnology + Orthopaedics). No prior DCF and no MEMORY.md entry -- first valuation. Not non-US, no FX, no NCI, SBC is material (not SBC-zero), so owner-fcf-adaptations.md was not required. FY0 = FY2025 (Dec year-end); year 1 of the projection is FY2026, which is already half reported (H1 revenue $12,609M, +6.1% reported; Q1 hit by the March-2026 cyberattack, Q2 +9.4%). Net debt is at 2026-06-30 (debt $750M current + $14,192M non-current = $14,942M; cash $3,391M + $85M current AFS debt securities), so roughly $0.3B of H1-2026 debt paydown overlaps the FY2026 flow -- under $1/share, accepted. INTEREST INCOME: $121M FY2025 is not stripped because the company is net-debt (net cash not material); the build is unlevered and net debt is deducted at the bridge. GROWTH is modelled ORGANIC (guidance 8.3-9.3% organic for FY2026) and acquisition spend is NOT deducted; Stryker is a serial acquirer (Inari $4.9B in 2025, ~$0.46B in H1 2026), so any M&A-driven revenue above these paths would have to be paid for in cash not in this model. EBITDA margin is GAAP EBITDA plus SBC (engine deducts SBC separately): FY2025 (6,459+243)/25,116 = 26.7%; H1-2026 (3,394+141)/12,609 = 28.0%. GAAP special items (restructuring, integration, recall/legal) are left in -- Stryker has them every year, so they are treated as a recurring cost rather than adjusted away; this is why the margin path sits ~3pp below the company's 'adjusted operating margin' framing (27.4% in Q2-26 before D&A). D&A 6.25% of revenue in FY2025 includes $732M of acquired-intangible amortization that runs off (schedule: $715M next 12m, ~$600M by year 5); the path glides D&A toward ~3.6%, just above capex, so the terminal year does not capitalize a tax shield from intangibles that only continued M&A would replenish. Working capital is negative capture (inventory- and receivables-heavy device maker: growth consumes cash). BUYBACKS: zero since FY2020 ($307M FY2019 last); FY2025 $1.03B authorization remaining and management signalled resumption in H2-2026 -- the flat count is currently a modelling convention not yet funded (diluted count drifted 380.3M FY2020 -> 386.0M).",
    "data_sources_note": "XBRL companyfacts (CIK 310764) pulled 2026-10-02 for debt split, AFS securities, equity-award taxes, interest income, intangible amortization schedule and diluted share count.",
